faqTitleEm: moving after a bereavement?
faqs:
- q: Can you help me move after my husband or wife has died?
  a: Yes. We help a surviving husband, wife or partner sort their belongings, decide what fits in a smaller or closer home, and then pack, move and settle in, with one dedicated coordinator and at a pace that suits them.
- q: How soon after a death should I move?
  a: There is no right time. It is your decision, made with your family and, where an estate is involved, the executor and the solicitor. We start when you are ready, and can work to shorter timescales if you need them.
- q: Can you help sort my loved one&rsquo;s belongings?
  a: Yes. We sort with you and your family, room by room. Nothing is disposed of without your agreement, and we help you decide what to keep, pass on or let go. We are not a house clearance firm, so we do not empty a property for disposal.
- q: Do you deal with probate or the legal side?
  a: No. We are not a probate service or legal advisers. Your solicitor or GOV.UK can explain probate, and our guide to <a href="/blog/moving-after-probate-clearing-a-loved-ones-home/">clearing a parent&rsquo;s house after a death</a> sets out the steps. See also <a href="/probate-house-clearance/">probate and moving help</a>.
- q: How much does it cost?
  a: Chayce packages start at {bronze} for packing and an insured removal. Silver Comfort at {silver} adds sorting and declutter help, a deep clean and unpacking with a coordinator. A Discovery Consultation costs {discovery}. The final price depends on the size of the home and is confirmed in writing before you book.
- q: Can my family be involved if they live far away?
  a: Yes. Moves are often arranged by adult children on a parent&rsquo;s behalf. They can be involved by phone or video, and your coordinator keeps everyone updated.
- q: Can you move me to a smaller home, a retirement village or closer to family?
  a: Yes. We help with <a href="/downsizing-help-for-elderly/">downsizing</a>, <a href="/retirement-village-removals/">retirement village moves</a> and long-distance moves closer to children or grandchildren. We do not recommend or sell properties.
- q: Is the removal insured?
  a: Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.
- q: Do you work outside Northampton?
  a: Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange moves across the whole UK.
